CONSTITUTION & BYLAWS

Our Governing Documents

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) is governed through its Constitution and Bylaws.

Together, these documents establish the formal structure of the organisation, its objectives, membership arrangements, governance processes and operational rules.

OCRA Constitution

The Constitution, also referred to within OCRA's governing documents as the Statutes, establishes the fundamental structure and purpose of the organisation.

It defines areas including:

- OCRA's name and legal form
- Purpose and objectives
- Activities
- Membership
- Governance structure
- General Assembly
- Management of the organisation
- Committees
- Finance
- Transparency and integrity
- Amendment procedures
- Dissolution

The Constitution establishes OCRA's objectives to:

- Promote, develop and govern obstacle sport throughout Ireland
- Represent Ireland in international obstacle sport
- Establish national standards for competition, coaching and Technical Officiating
- Organise National Championships and qualification pathways
- Support athletes, clubs, coaches and Technical Officials
- Promote integrity, fairness, athlete welfare and inclusion
- Work with national and international sporting organisations

