OCRA Bylaws

The Bylaws provide the operational rules through which the principles contained within the Constitution are implemented.

They cover areas including:

- Membership procedures
- Member rights and responsibilities
- General Assembly procedures
- Organisational management
- Committees
- Technical Officials
- Coaching
- Disciplinary processes
- Event standards
- Communication and records
- Amendment procedures

The Bylaws supplement the Constitution and should be interpreted consistently with it.

